==English==

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|frm|réviser}}, from {{der|en|la|revīsō}}, from {{m|la|re-}} + {{m|la|vīsō||examine}}, frequentative of {{m|la|videō||see}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ɹɪˈvaɪz/|a=RP}}
* {{IPA|en|/ɹɪˈvaɪz/|/ɹəˈvaɪz/|a=UK,GA,CA}}
** {{audio|en|En-us-revise.ogg|a=California}}
* {{IPA|en|/ɹɪˈvɑez/|/ɹəˈvɑez/|a=AU}}
** {{audio|en|en-au-revise.ogg|a=Queensland}}
* {{IPA|en|/ɹəˈvaɪ̯z/|[ɹəˈvɑe̯z]|a=NZ}}
* {{rhymes|en|aɪz|s=2}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# To [[review]], [[alter]] and [[amend]], especially of written material.
#: {{ux|en|This statute should be '''revised'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1951|author=[[w:Muhammad Ali (writer)|Maulana Muhammad Ali]]|title=Preface to the '''Revised''' Edition: The Holy Quran: English Translation and Commentary|pageurl=http://books.google.com.au/books?id=Po2BO-TsMosC&pg=PT34&dq=%22revise%22%7C%22revising%22%7C%22revised%22+-intitle:%22revise%7Crevised%7Crevising%22+-inauthor:%22%22&hl=en&sa=X&ei=OIAKUM7WOIagiQe3x8S1DQ&redir_esc=y#v=onepage&q=%22revise%22%7C%22revising%22%7C%22revised%22%20-intitle%3A%22revise%7Crevised%7Crevising%22%20-inauthor%3A%22%22&f=false|page=unnumbered|year_published=2011
|passage=There has been a demand for a '''revised''' edition of my English Translation and Commentary of the Holy Qur′an since the end of the Second World War.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2008|author=Wayne C. Booth; Gregory G. Colomb; Joseph M. Williams.|title=The Craft of Research|edition=3rd|pageurl=http://books.google.com.au/books?id=Y31pUtkwb2oC&pg=PA203&dq=%22revise%22%7C%22revising%22%7C%22revised%22+-intitle:%22revise%7Crevised%7Crevising%22+-inauthor:%22%22&hl=en&sa=X&ei=OIAKUM7WOIagiQe3x8S1DQ&redir_esc=y#v=onepage&q=%22revise%22%7C%22revising%22%7C%22revised%22%20-intitle%3A%22revise%7Crevised%7Crevising%22%20-inauthor%3A%22%22&f=false|page=203|publisher=University of Chicago Press
|passage=The best writers know better. They write a first draft not to show readers, but to discover what case they can make for their point and whether it stands up to their own scrutiny. Then they '''revise''' and '''revise''' until they think their readers will think so too.}}
# {{lb|en|UK|Australia|New Zealand}} To look over again (something previously written or learned), especially in preparation for an [[examination]].
#: {{syn|en|review|q=US, Canada}}
#: {{ux|en|I've only just begun to '''revise''' for my exams.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1957|author=Clifford Thomas Morgan; James Deese|title=How to Study|publisher=McGraw-Hill|pageurl=http://books.google.com.au/books?id=VYhqAAAAMAAJ&q=%22In+revising+your+notes,+you+can+also+reorganize+them%22&dq=%22In+revising+your+notes,+you+can+also+reorganize+them%22&hl=en&sa=X&ei=EZoKUPnQKaaiiAet5uS1DQ&ved=0CDIQ6AEwAA|page=16
|passage=In '''revising''' your notes, you can also reorganize them so that they are more legible, better arranged, and in a more useful condition for subsequent reviews.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2003|author=Stuart Redman|title=English Vocabulary in Use: Pre-Intermediate & Intermediate|edition=2nd|pageurl=http://books.google.com.au/books?id=thKKgYei8XsC&pg=PA5&dq=%22revise%22%7C%22revising%22%7C%22revised%22+study+OR+exam+-intitle:%22revise%7Crevised%7Crevising%22+-inauthor:%22%22&hl=en&sa=X&ei=iJkKUKfCNOuaiQf8mdG1DQ&redir_esc=y#v=onepage&q=%22revise%22%7C%22revising%22%7C%22revised%22%20study%20OR%20exam%20-intitle%3A%22revise%7Crevised%7Crevising%22%20-inauthor%3A%22%22&f=false|page=5|publisher=Cambridge University Press
|passage=4 Is it necessary to '''revise''' vocabulary (= study it again for a second or third time)?<br>5 Is it better to '''revise''' vocabulary occasionally for long periods of time, or is it better to '''revise''' regularly for short periods of time?}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} To look at again, to reflect on.

